# Camera masters. Nothing on the site loads them: the pages serve the
# compressed .web.mp4 copies, which ARE tracked. Keep these safe locally (or
# put the repo on Git LFS if they need to live alongside the code).
#
# The first three are each past GitHub's 100MB limit for a single file - a push
# fails outright with them included. sos.mp4 is under it, but it is a master
# like the others and there is no reason to carry sixty megabytes of it when
# what the page loads is five.
video/x3_1.mp4
video/reel 011.mp4
video/x4.mp4
video/sos.mp4

# Source material: the shoots the site is drawn from, and a transfer dump.
# Several gigabytes between them, and nothing here serves any of it - what the
# pages load are the copies in pics/ and video/. Named so that a stray add
# cannot sweep them into the history, which is not something a repository
# recovers from easily.
portfolio/
transfer-01a06f70/

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Local scratch
.tools/
*.log
.claude*

# Node. package.json is tracked so the Puppeteer-based checks can be set up
# again with one install; the installed tree itself has no business in here.
node_modules/

# Python bytecode from scripts/build-works-media.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Throwaway verification harnesses and the screenshots they leave behind.
# They drive a local server with Puppeteer and are not part of the site.
verify-*.mjs
tmp-*
shot-*.png

# Files taken out of the site during the cleanup, kept locally only.
_archive/
